            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Augment element (200) for femoral applications in a knee prosthesis, the augment element (200) comprising a metal body (201) of a substantially truncated conical shape configured to be inserted into a bone extremity and having an outer surface comprising a metal trabecular surface (202). The metal body (201) is hollow with an axial through-cavity (204) defining a plurality of substantially annular transversal sections. The metal body (201) is inclined in a direction of inclination, so as to define at least one eccentricity between a first transversal section (205) at a first end of the axial through-cavity (204) and a second transversal section (206) at a second end of the axial through-cavity (204). The first transversal section (205) is smaller in size with respect to the second transversal section (206). The augment element (200) further comprises a pair of bicondylar supports (220a, 220b) arranged sideways in the metal body (201), each of the bicondylar supports (220a, 220b) protruding from the second transversal section (206) and comprising a tapered body widening away from the metal body (201).</p>
            </abstract>
